    "description": "Render operator and partner logos. Two fields per object: a Logo URL holding the link, and an image render off it.\n\n=== FIELDS ===\n\n* Logo URL — Logo_URL__c — URL — lives in the More Info tab\n\n* Logo — image render off Logo_URL__c\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Mechanism per Kobi: 'you have to upload the file somewhere and then get the link and put it in the logo URL and that will basically show it as an image.'\n\n* Only BetMGM and DraftKings have test logos today; the rest need populating.\n\n* CLIENT ACTION, still outstanding: WagerTech is sending the logo files. Joyce: 'why don't we send you the files, and then ideally it's not something we ever have to configure... anytime you have a new operator, it's part of setting up that operator.' Not received as of Aug 17.\n\n* Add logo population to the operator/partner setup runbook so it happens once per new record.\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* Emily initially waved off a Partner logo ('if it's a pain in the ass to upload, then I would just not care'); Joyce reinstated it. Build for both.\n\n* Kobi's doc comment Aug 13: 'This would be actual images and would require a Logo URL Field to go along with it.'\n\n* Relevant to the squash question — Kobi argued on Aug 17 that 'a logo URL, those are all important things for them to configure', which is the case for keeping the System section rather than deleting it.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Taryn doc OP-1 / PT-1\n\n* Aug 13 call\n\n* Kobi doc comment Aug 13\n\n* Aug 17 call\n\nDependencies: BUILD-126, BUILD-136\n\nOwner (proposed): TBD\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nCreated 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
